<h2 id="domestic-asset-anchoring-and-housing-prices">Domestic Asset Anchoring and Housing Prices</h2>

<p><strong>Key takeaways for this sections:</strong></p>

<h3 id="housing-prices-and-interest-rates">Housing Prices and Interest Rates</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Irrational Debt in the Private Sector: The significant increase in housing prices over the past decade has led to substantial inflation of credit within the sector, causing market dynamics to deviate from the nationwide Return on Assets (ROA) level.</li>
  <li><strong>Shadow bank system enlarge the probleem</strong> Beyond the debt issued by private sectors to the commerical banks, the shadow banking system has been a major source of credit in the real estate market.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="relationship-between-housing-prices-and-government-bond-yields">Relationship Between Housing Prices and Government Bond Yields</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Housing Prices</strong>: Heavily influenced by buyer income levels and expectations.</li>
  <li><strong>Government Bond Yields</strong>: Serve as the benchmark for overall asset yields. When housing yields fall below government bond yields, the attractiveness of real estate investment decreases.</li>
</ul>

<p>Over the past decade, China’s real estate market has experienced a surge driven by a Fear of Missing Out (FOMO) among buyers, 
further fueled by relatively nationwide low interest rates, which compared to the expectation of asset price increase.</p>

